# The build context is now the repo root, which holds 3.7GB of manifests, a
# virtualenv and DB backups -- none of which the image needs. Deny everything,
# then allow back exactly what docker/Dockerfile COPYs.
*
!pyproject.toml
!README.md
!src/
!dags/
# docker/ itself must be un-excluded before a nested negation can reach into
# it (Docker skips negated files under an already-excluded directory), so
# this re-excludes everything else under docker/ (e.g. postgres-init/) right
# back after opening the directory up.
!docker
docker/*
!docker/start-with-init.sh
